        <history>
          <p>Nielsen's only violin concerto combines a Baroque-influenced two-movement design (each divided into a slow introduction and fast main section) with a soloistic style rooted in his own early career as an orchestral violinist. It remains a cornerstone of the Danish violin repertoire, if still underplayed internationally.</p>
